<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ===================================================================================
         V1 BASELINE (SCRUM-107, owner directive 2026-08-08). The mandate transition audit
         trail, owned by MRG, which also owns the derived views, the mandate_override sink
         and the delta/watermark machinery.

         Under derivation there is no transition EVENT: state is an aggregate over all legs.
         The transition is the DELTA between man_watermark.last_state (the last state this
         client was told) and the currently derived mandate_current_status.state, which is
         exactly what a report window already computes, so the append rides the same
         observation that writes the delivery ledger row (see ManAdvanceRecorder).

         THE FINAL SHAPE IS MINTED ONCE, HERE. The previous version of this file reached the
         same shape in five steps, because the table already stood on a deployed cluster in
         an older shape: a guarded create, two dropNotNullConstraint changesets each probing
         nullability through an information_schema sqlCheck, an addColumn for report_id, and
         a drop-then-add swapping the unique key. All five are gone. A v1 database has no
         older shape to converge, so the columns are simply declared nullable and the
         identity key is simply declared correctly, and the sqlCheck preconditions those
         steps needed disappear with them.

         Two shape decisions survive from that history and are still right:

         1. source_leg and response_file are NULLABLE and stay NULL on every derived row.
            They carry no value under derivation. They are kept rather than dropped because
            the audit trail is the one place a future non-derived writer would record leg
            evidence, and a nullable column costs nothing.
         2. The identity is (mandate_ref, to_state, report_id), NOT (mandate_ref, to_state,
            response_file). The latter guards nothing once response_file is NULL, because
            NULLs do not collide in a unique index on CRDB or Postgres. Keying on the report
            window mirrors man_delivery_ledger's (client, mandate_ref, state), so replaying a
            window is a zero-duplicate no-op.

         mandate_status_history has exactly ONE creator, MRG, so no changeset here carries a
         MARK_RAN guard.
         =================================================================================== -->

    <changeSet id="008-man-status-history" author="dcre">
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not><tableExists tableName="mandate_status_history"/></not>
        </preConditions>
        
        <createTable tableName="mandate_status_history">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="mandate_ref" type="VARCHAR(35)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <!-- Previous reported state, or REQUESTED on a first observation: MSR's documented
                 implicit start state (MandateState javadoc), never a persisted projection state. -->
            <column name="from_state" type="VARCHAR(16)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <column name="to_state" type="VARCHAR(16)"><constraints nullable="false"/></column>
            <!-- NULL on every derived row. See the file header. -->
            <column name="source_leg" type="VARCHAR(16)"/>
            <column name="reason_code" type="VARCHAR(8)"/>
            <!-- NULL on every derived row; see source_leg. -->
            <column name="response_file" type="VARCHAR(128)"/>
            <!-- The report window the transition was observed in: the third leg of the identity. -->
            <column name="report_id" type="UUID"/>
            <column name="at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <createIndex tableName="mandate_status_history" indexName="ix_man_status_history_ref">
            <column name="mandate_ref"/>
        </createIndex>
        <!-- The derived full identity, declared with the table rather than swapped in later.
             See the file header for why it keys on report_id and not response_file. -->
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="mandate_status_history"
                             columnNames="mandate_ref, to_state, report_id"
                             constraintName="uq_man_status_history_derived"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
